voltj...@gmail.com wrote:
>
> --Flint stones from a sling do double the damage of ordinary rocks,
> but are difficult to find. Is there even any way to get them in
> quantities apart from wishing?

Gems do the same damage as rocks but weigh 1/10th
as much as rocks.  There are plenty of worthless glass
gems around.  The way to get more flint stones is to
polypile and polypiling generates far more glass than
flint.  There's a nearly unlimited supply of rocks and
rocks polypile into glass or other minerals.

> --And for my last question, shurikens and boomerangs. They're very
> nice, but given how hard it is to get them in any quantity, as well as
> their propensity to break when thrown, is training either to skill to
> expert even a feasible proposition?

I've enhanced shuriken to basic with a samurai just for fun.
They aren't common enough to get much farther though
you can do it with polypiling.  Per the usual rules for
disappearing missiles if they are blessed and your luck
is maxed a goodly stack of them can last a long time.
But their damage to weight and damage to multifire ratios
aren't that much better than daggers or arrows so they
aren't worth the effort except for fun.


